route-app-server-shared-runtime-to-harness

Lane: normalization

Unit: route-app-server-runtime-to-harness

ChildPatch: route-app-server-shared-runtime-to-harness

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Keep app-server daemon coordination and disposable runtime state under CODEX_HARNESS, separate from durable CODEX_HOME data.

Requires: Unit:normalization/normalize-base-roots-for-processes

Provides: Route shared UID socket rendezvous, control sockets, startup locks, recovery, daemon state and their CLI, TUI, telemetry, and fixture consumers to harness; propagate the selected harness into Linux sandbox execution while preserving socket ownership and isolation checks.

Boundary: Home retains configuration, durable data, and installed binaries; base-root selection belongs to normalize-base-roots-for-processes, and thread writer state and sandbox mount policy retain their own owners.

Verification: uds daemon_directory tests, app-server-transport unix_socket_tests, app-server daemon tests, managed remote-control persistence and lock tests, TUI daemon compatibility, and sandboxing manager tests exercise root separation, coordination paths, permissions, executor propagation, and unchanged lifecycle behavior.


